Z||000000||chris6878||02-28-2000||12:13 AM||||Well....<P>My engine fan wasnt coming on at all....  I was planning on putting a toggle switch in when it got closer to summer...  Well.. last night my 85 SE V6 got a little warm past 220. And my car started Vibrating really bad.. I didnt know what was going on... <P>I turn off the engine..  The car still is vibrating...  come to find it out.. the engine fan finally decided to kick on ( a little late) and its seems to be going at a high speed and its vibrating the hole car. This is the first time the engine has been this warm... so i know now that the fan does work...<P>So...   Question 1. why isnt it comming on when it should..?<BR>        Question 2. why is it vibrating when it is on?<P>thanks.<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||02-28-2000||12:54 AM||||Sounds like it is out of balance. Check for things like a missing blade, blade loose on the motor shaft, whole assembly loose, etc.<P>Just to be safe... I would recommend disconnecting the battery ground before sticking your hand down into the fan area.||||reg||1
